I reviewed PR #177 (head `689b9fe`, base `pi-exa-guided/prototype`). These findings come from reading the code only; none was confirmed by running a test.

```json
[
  {
    "file": "packages/pi-exa/extensions/cycle-pi.ts",
    "line": 510,
    "summary": "researchMode=submit with no active cycle and no cycleId skips every guided check and runs as a blocking standalone paid Agent run; only researchMode=active gets the `!record` guard.",
    "failure_scenario": "No cycle is active and the assistant calls web_research_exa {researchMode:'submit', proposalId:'abc', query:'x'}. record is undefined, so line 508 (it checks only cycleId/expectedRevision), line 510 (active only) and line 511 (`record &&`) are all skipped. researchMode and proposalId are stripped and tool.execute runs performResearch: a paid, polling Agent run with no dialog and no proposal. That is exactly the 'guided request falls back to standalone' case the PR says it prevents. The test only covers this case with an active cycle (line 481 of the test)."
  },
  {
    "file": "packages/pi-exa/extensions/cycle-pi.ts",
    "line": 561,
    "summary": "Guided submit shows the spending dialog and durably writes the grant plus the one-use permission before checking whether reserveAgent can succeed at all.",
    "failure_scenario": "The cycle already has an attempt: a not-dispatched first submit (status back to planning), a failed run, or SUBMISSION_UNKNOWN. assertDraft allows all of these, so preview and buildProposal succeed. The operator approves 'Submits exactly one Exa Agent run', grantDialogApproval raises the lifetime ceiling and records the permission, then reserveAgent throws AGENT_ATTEMPT_EXISTS (research-cycles.ts:822). The same happens with an unpermitted unknown liability (ExplorationApprovalError UNKNOWN_LIABILITY). Each time, consent is recorded for spending that could never be dispatched, and the operator can be prompted again on every retry. The test at line 432 does not assert that confirm was not called."
  },
  {
    "file": "packages/pi-exa/extensions/cycle-pi.ts",
    "line": 615,
    "summary": "The SUBMISSION_NOT_DISPATCHED text says to 'approve and submit again explicitly', but no later researchMode=submit can ever succeed for this cycle.",
    "failure_scenario": "The create is not dispatched (deadline hit before the guard, pre-dispatch abort, or submitter missing). finish() marks the attempt not-dispatched but leaves it in record.attempts. When the assistant follows the guidance and calls submit again, it gets another dialog and another grant write, then AGENT_ATTEMPT_EXISTS. The guided flow is stuck and the message does not mention researchMode=retry."
  },
  {
    "file": "packages/pi-exa/extensions/cycle-pi.ts",
    "line": 578,
    "summary": "The submitter is resolved only after the dialog, the grant write and the attempt reservation; the `!submissionFactory` preflight never catches a factory that returns undefined.",
    "failure_scenario": "web_research_exa is disabled by config, so researchFactory's isToolEnabled returns false and submissionFactory returns undefined. The operator approves, grants are written and reserveAgent freezes an attempt. Only then does `if (!submitter) throw` fire. finish() marks the attempt not-dispatched and the cycle is permanently blocked from guided submission (AGENT_ATTEMPT_EXISTS), all for a configuration that should have been refused before the dialog."
  },
  {
    "file": "packages/pi-exa/extensions/research-cycles.ts",
    "line": 790,
    "summary": "Dialog grants use a ceiling and tool scope computed before a dialog that can stay open for 10 minutes. Because the latest grant wins, a grant made in the meantime is silently overwritten (the same applies to the exploration grantBudget call at cycle-pi.ts:755).",
    "failure_scenario": "The assistant issues an exploratory web_search_exa and a submit in parallel. Both dialogs compute tools/ceiling from the same empty grant set: [web_search_exa]/$X and [web_research_exa]/$Y. If the exploration approval is written last, the latest grant lacks web_research_exa and has the smaller ceiling, so reserveAgent fails SCOPE_APPROVAL_REQUIRED after the operator approved. The same thing happens if an operator `/exa-research approve` raises the ceiling during the dialog: the dialog grant lowers it again. The fix is to merge with the current latest grant inside the write transaction."
  },
  {
    "file": "packages/pi-exa/extensions/cycle-pi.ts",
    "line": 729,
    "summary": "The exploration-dialog eligibility check ignores OVERSPEND and conflicting receipts that the reason priority hides, and buildProposal never checks them, so a scope dialog quietly raises the ceiling above an overspend.",
    "failure_scenario": "Reported spend is above the latest ceiling and the tool is out of scope. assessExploration returns SCOPE_APPROVAL_REQUIRED, because that reason is checked before OVERSPEND. blockedOperationIds is empty, so the dialog path runs and sets the ceiling to max(ceiling, exposure+proposed). An overspend that the 'simple scope/ceiling cases only' comment says should stay on operator commands is cleared by a one-click dialog. buildProposal does the same for Agent submits."
  },
  {
    "file": "packages/pi-exa/extensions/research-proposal.ts",
    "line": 47,
    "summary": "For fixed-price effort, the dialog's one-use allowance equals the base published price only, excluding contact/provider add-ons, while assessAgent treats the exact-request permission as covering 'possible contact/provider costs'.",
    "failure_scenario": "The plan has dataSources providers at medium effort. The estimate and allowance come out at $0.10, the ceiling is raised to exposure+$0.10, and the run is funded although provider charges can push actual cost well above the approved allowance. Previously the operator set the allowance explicitly with approve-request, so the provider cost could be priced in."
  },
  {
    "file": "packages/pi-exa/extensions/web-research.ts",
    "line": 874,
    "summary": "When the deadline expires before the dispatch guard, the code throws AgentSubmissionUnacknowledgedError ('dispatched… outcome unknown') even though nothing was sent.",
    "failure_scenario": "beforeCreate's durable write takes longer than --exa-submit-timeout-ms. The error says Exa 'did not acknowledge' and that the outcome is unknown. finish() correctly marks the attempt not-dispatched, so the result reads 'SUBMISSION_NOT_DISPATCHED: … (Exa did not acknowledge the Agent run … outcome is unknown …)', which contradicts itself in text shown to the user and the model."
  },
  {
    "file": "packages/pi-exa/extensions/web-research.ts",
    "line": 851,
    "summary": "submitResearchRun copies performResearch's budget validation, createParams construction, observer fence and create/raw chain almost line for line, and tools.ts:652-684 duplicates the ResearchParams mapping for submit and perform.",
    "failure_scenario": "Two copies of the request-building and dispatch-fence logic must stay in sync. A future change to createParams (a new field, a beta header, a stricter fence) applied to only one copy would make guided submissions send a different request than the one that was hashed and approved. A shared buildCreateParams/dispatchCreate helper and a single `researchParams` object in tools.ts would remove the duplication."
  },
  {
    "file": "packages/pi-exa/extensions/cycle-pi.ts",
    "line": 737,
    "summary": "The exploration dialog re-implements buildProposal's exposure and ceiling formula, and the submit path re-reads the cycle from disk up to three times in a row and calls view(closed) twice.",
    "failure_scenario": "The approval-ceiling rule (roundUpCents(max(ceiling, reported+pending+assessedUnknown+proposed)) plus the merged tools) now lives in two places and can drift, so the two dialogs could show different ceilings. The submit path also does redundant inspect() disk reads (lines 586, 597 and 620). A shared approvalFigures(assessment, proposed, tool) helper and a single post-execute inspect would fix both."
  }
]
```

