    "summary": "registerMissing never re-registers tools already registered at factory time, so `--exa-timeout-ms` and `--exa-research-timeout-ms` (read through resolvePiTimeouts before Pi applies flags) are never applied to them.",
    "failure_scenario": "`pi -e npm:@feniix/pi-exa -- --exa-timeout-ms 5000` with cycles off: at factory time getFlag('exa-timeout-ms') returns undefined, so web_search_exa/web_fetch_exa/web_answer_exa/web_find_similar_exa (and web_research_exa when enabled by config) are created with timeouts=undefined. Tools are built once with their options (createExaTools: `timeoutFor = () => resolveExaToolTimeoutMs(name, opts.timeouts)`). At session_start the rebuilt tools that do carry the flag timeouts are skipped by `!registered.has(tool.name)`. Calls keep the built-in 60000/180000 ms timeouts, so the flags this PR says are now reachable still have no effect."
  },
  {
    "file": "packages/pi-exa/extensions/index.ts",
    "line": 147,
    "summary": "Tools enabled by the factory-time config (default config path or env) stay registered even when the config from `--exa-config-file` disables them. In cycles mode those leftovers keep their raw registration and never get the cycle wrapper.",
    "failure_scenario": "The smoke's own setup: the default config enables all default tools, then `--exa-config-file ../exa.json` sets enabledTools to [planner tools, web_search_exa, web_research_exa]. web_fetch_exa, web_answer_exa and web_find_similar_exa were registered at factory time and are never removed. With `--exa-enable-cycles`, `registerPiTools(registration, tools)` only re-wraps the 6 allowed tools. The other 3 paid tools stay callable without CYCLE_GUIDELINES or the cycle's paid-parameter gating, and the user's allowlist is silently ignored."
  },
  {
    "file": "packages/pi-exa/extensions/index.ts",
    "line": 152,
    "summary": "Each buildTools() call runs createExaTools without a shared planner, so each call creates a new createResearchPlanner(). Planner tools registered at factory time and planner tools first registered at session_start therefore use different in-memory planners.",
    "failure_scenario": "The default config has enabledTools ['exa_research_step','web_search_exa'] and `--exa-config-file` enables all planner tools. exa_research_step stays on planner A (factory), while exa_research_status/summary/reset are newly registered from planner B (session_start). Steps recorded by the model never show up in status or summary, which report an empty plan."
