    "failure_scenario": "A user still passing `--exa-config ~/exa.json` gets '[pi-exa] --exa-config is deprecated…' written to the console on every Exa tool call (resolveApiKey → resolveAuth → getResolvedConfig) and on every session_start. In the interactive TUI this repeatedly prints raw text over the rendered UI. Before this PR the warning never fired."
  },
  {
    "file": "packages/pi-exa/__tests__/guided-smoke.rpc.test.ts",
    "line": 148,
    "summary": "`pi.waitFor(record => record.type === 'message_update')` resolves immediately on message_update records from earlier turns, because waitFor first checks `this.records.find(predicate)`. The 'completion during an active streamed reply' sync point does not actually wait for anything.",
    "failure_scenario": "The earlier research turns already produced message_update records (the faux provider streams at 80 tokens/s). server.complete() therefore runs right after the long prompt is written to stdin, possibly before Pi starts the turn. With a 50 ms monitor interval the notice can land before the long reply begins, so `kinds.lastIndexOf('assistant', noticeIndex)` picks the wrong message and the 'long digression' assertion fails intermittently. When it passes, it may not have exercised the queued-during-stream path at all."
