    "failure_scenario": "'--exa-timeout-ms surfaces the configured timeout' passes because getFlag('exa-timeout-ms') returns '75' during exaExtension(). Under real Pi it returns undefined at that point, and the session_start path never re-registers web_search_exa (finding 1). The one new ordering-aware test only checks that a newly enabled tool appears; it does not check refreshed timeouts or tools that should drop out."
  },
  {
    "file": "packages/pi-exa/extensions/index.ts",
    "line": 140,
    "summary": "Altitude: tracking a 'register only what is missing' set treats the symptom (flags arrive late). The deeper fix is to resolve timeouts and enablement when a tool executes, or to re-register the full tool set at session_start.",
    "failure_scenario": "The diffing approach is why findings 1–3 exist: anything decided at factory time (timeouts, the allowlist, planner identity) can't be corrected later. A simpler fix: make ExaToolsOptions.timeouts a resolver (`() => resolvePiTimeouts(pi)`; timeoutFor is already a thunk) and do all registration in session_start with one shared planner, letting Pi's same-name registerTool override. Separately, buildTools() rebuilds every tool and a new planner on each session_start (new/switch/fork) only to throw most of them away."
