    "failure_scenario": "The pi child is slow to exit after stdin closes, for example while a background monitor is persisting a write. kill() sends SIGTERM, rm(scratch, {recursive}) runs at the same time, and a late write can cause ENOTEMPTY or recreate files. afterEach swallows the error, so exa-rpc-pi-* temp directories leak. The follow-up commit 75c7a51 (retry scratch directory removal while an in-flight monitor write finishes) suggests this race is real."
  },
  {
