    "line": 126,
    "summary": "counts() counts every GET as `gets`, including GETs to unexpected paths that the handler answers with 405, so the smoke's `other: 0` assertions cannot catch unexpected GET endpoints.",
    "failure_scenario": "A regression makes the guided flow call GET /research/v1/... or any other unplanned GET endpoint. The mock returns 405, but the request is counted in `gets` instead of `other`. `expect(server.counts()).toMatchObject({ creates: 1, other: 0 })` still passes, so the 'no other Exa endpoint' guarantee isn't checked. Separately, JSON.parse(text) in the async handler has no guard, so a malformed body becomes an unhandled rejection."
  },
  {
    "file": "packages/pi-exa/extensions/exa-client.ts",
    "line": 35,
    "summary": "resolveExaBaseUrl accepts any non-empty string without checking for a scheme or that it parses as a URL. exa-js joins it directly (`this.baseURL + endpoint`), so a mistyped value fails with an unclear error, and the API key goes to whatever host is configured.",
